Phase 2 run #1: INVALID, gate not applied; fix root causes

600 calls completed but 103 failed (41 HTTP 429, 62 reasoning-truncation).
The failures were not random: the harness processed all positives then all
negatives, so accumulating rate-limit pressure struck the back half. For
English, 41 of 41 failures landed on negatives. Failed verdicts fail OPEN, so
each was scored as a false answer -- English B false-answer inflated
0.2034 to 0.5300 and balanced accuracy depressed 0.7083 to 0.5450 by call
ORDER alone.

That swing can reverse the verdict, so the pre-registered rule was NOT applied
in either direction and Phase 3 is NOT unlocked.

Fixes:
- shuffle the two classes together so failures are class-independent
- retry backoff 0.3s/3s/3 attempts to 2s/30s/5 attempts (sized for rate limits)
- judge max_tokens 1500 to 3000 (reasoning tail still truncating)
- harness records judge_failure_rate/results_trustworthy, warns above 2%

Contaminated numbers, latency percentiles and diagnosis in EXPERIMENTS.md E14.
177 tests pass.

